00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:59,460
Underwear will return on Modern Marvels.

307
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:06,040
The main thing we demand of underwear is simply comfort.

308
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:09,360
But the Wickers brand delivers much more,

309
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:11,860
and the proof is in the polyester material,

310
00:23:12,180 --> 00:23:15,420
which is made here at Beverly Knits in Gastonia, North Carolina.

311
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:20,560
Wickers works for you while you're working up a sweat.

312
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,600
They do this using a process called wicking,

313
00:23:25,601 --> 00:23:28,060
which defines so-called performance underwear.

314
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,880
The whole idea of performance is moisture management,

315
00:23:32,881 --> 00:23:34,220
moisture wicking.

316
00:23:34,221 --> 00:23:38,480
The ability to move moisture away from your body

317
00:23:38,481 --> 00:23:41,160
to keep you dry and therefore keep you warmer

318
00:23:41,161 --> 00:23:42,560
and more comfortable.

319
00:23:42,561 --> 00:23:45,440
You had a lot of people who experienced hyperthermia

320
00:23:45,441 --> 00:23:47,620
because you're out there, it's cold,

321
00:23:47,621 --> 00:23:51,360
you're sweating still and it just sticks to you.

322
00:23:51,361 --> 00:23:53,900
With this fabric, it just keeps moving moisture,

323
00:23:53,901 --> 00:23:57,100
and it retains heat so you won't get cold.

324
00:23:57,101 --> 00:23:59,340
In some cases, you want to be kept cool,

325
00:23:59,341 --> 00:24:01,360
and that helps during the summertime too

326
00:24:01,361 --> 00:24:04,760
because the evaporation of your perspiration

327
00:24:04,761 --> 00:24:08,540
is creating an air conditioning feel on your body.

328
00:24:09,780 --> 00:24:11,800
This is an experiment of moisture management.

329
00:24:11,801 --> 00:24:14,680
This is a single fabric that's just folded over.

330
00:24:14,681 --> 00:24:17,160
The part of the fabric against the body

331
00:24:17,161 --> 00:24:19,460
and the part of the fabric that's away from the body.

332
00:24:19,461 --> 00:24:23,980
So against the body, as you have moisture,

333
00:24:23,981 --> 00:24:26,140
you'll see it goes in almost immediately.

334
00:24:26,141 --> 00:24:29,440
On the other side, again, now that's the same fabric,

335
00:24:29,441 --> 00:24:33,860
but that water will sit there for quite a while.

336
00:24:33,861 --> 00:24:36,060
How does wickers manage this trick?

337
00:24:36,061 --> 00:24:39,300
A big factor is how the polyester is knitted.

338
00:24:39,301 --> 00:24:41,340
This form of knitting is good for the wicking

339
00:24:41,341 --> 00:24:44,060
because we have denier gradient yarns.

340
00:24:44,061 --> 00:24:48,520
We have one yarn that has a lot more filaments or little fibers

341
00:24:48,521 --> 00:24:49,980
than the other yarn.

342
00:24:50,080 --> 00:24:52,120
And so the yarn that's got the fewer fibers

343
00:24:52,220 --> 00:24:53,660
are next to the skin.

344
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:56,560
The yarn that's got the more fibers are on the outside.

345
00:24:56,660 --> 00:24:59,360
And that pulls the moisture through the fabric

346
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:01,660
and spreads the moisture up into the garment.

347
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:05,340
And then it evaporates and cools the hiker or skier

348
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:09,640
or soldier or whatever down as they're doing their activities.

349
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:11,680
But there's another secret to making this moisture

350
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:15,640
movement fabric, which occurs at another site.

351
00:25:15,740 --> 00:25:18,520
As machines dye the material, it's

352
00:25:18,521 --> 00:25:23,600
It's called Aquatec, a proprietary chemical procedure that actually changes the molecular

353
00:25:23,601 --> 00:25:26,460
structure of the polyester fabric.

354
00:25:26,461 --> 00:25:31,120
The fabric requires this special treatment because without it, it's hydrophobic, meaning

355
00:25:31,121 --> 00:25:33,340
it doesn't absorb water.

356
00:25:33,341 --> 00:25:36,080
It becomes a totally different molecule.

357
00:25:36,081 --> 00:25:43,320
And the molecule that comes out will wick away water or other substances and also dry

358
00:25:43,321 --> 00:25:44,320
really fast.

359
00:25:44,321 --> 00:25:52,480
So the chemical changes the polyester from a non-absorbent man-made fiber into an absorbent man-made fiber.

360
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:57,240
Then the wicking that's applied will last for the life of the garment.

361
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:06,240
Beverly Knits also manufactures another line of Wickers underwear that not only moves moisture, but is also fire resistant.

362
00:26:06,241 --> 00:26:13,620
The Rickers team developed this product in 2003 for forest firefighters in the western

363
00:26:13,621 --> 00:26:14,863
United States.

364
00:26:14,864 --> 00:26:21,700
The company later learned it could be of invaluable use to America's military

365
00:26:21,701 --> 00:26:22,948
forces in Iraq.

366
00:26:22,949 --> 00:26:29,520
Wounded soldiers were experiencing life-threatening complications caused by the

367
00:26:29,521 --> 00:26:32,340
standard polyester t-shirts they wore under their uniforms.

368
00:26:32,341 --> 00:26:38,780
This Marine Corps surgeon, Captain Welling, was operating in the field, would notice that

369
00:26:38,781 --> 00:26:44,020
the burn injuries had been exasperated by the melting of the polyester.

370
00:26:44,021 --> 00:26:50,220
So he had to first surgically remove the melted polyester from the body before he could begin

371
00:26:50,221 --> 00:26:56,180
any surgery on the burns that were inflicted to begin with.

372
00:26:56,181 --> 00:27:01,800
Wicker's fire-resistant fabric consists of two different yarns.

373
00:27:01,801 --> 00:27:04,429
is a fine wool made from merino sheep.

374
00:27:04,430 --> 00:27:07,680
The other is a form of rayon made from wood and

375
00:27:07,681 --> 00:27:11,380
treated with silica, a natural fire retardant.

376
00:27:11,381 --> 00:27:14,920
So this wool is made of the best wool in the

377
00:27:14,921 --> 00:27:21,140
world. It's imported from Europe. And this rayon fiber allows the fabric to, when it

378
00:27:21,141 --> 00:27:24,816
burns, to char and not cause it to melt to the skin.

379
00:27:24,817 --> 00:27:27,220
What we're going to do is show you

380
00:27:27,221 --> 00:27:31,214
a test of flammability. Now this is a normal piece of polyester not treated.

381
00:27:31,215 --> 00:27:31,915
And you'll

382
00:27:31,916 --> 00:27:33,740
see it'll burn and then drip.

383
00:27:33,741 --> 00:27:36,180
And that's normal polyester.

384
00:27:36,181 --> 00:27:39,900
This is a Wickers fabric that's inherently flame retardant.

385
00:27:39,901 --> 00:27:43,480
When ignited, the wool and rayon material chars,

386
00:27:43,481 --> 00:27:47,040
but the smoky emission is non-toxic.

387
00:27:47,041 --> 00:27:48,780
This sets the Wickers material apart

388
00:27:48,781 --> 00:27:51,640
from many conventional fire-resistant fabrics,

389
00:27:51,641 --> 00:27:54,860
like this one made from a type of acrylic that doesn't burn,

