449
00:32:24,021 --> 00:32:27,520
But here, we do keep up with all of them.

450
00:32:27,521 --> 00:32:33,080
Any given pair of socks might have as many as 10 different fibers woven in.

451
00:32:33,081 --> 00:32:38,360
Everything from cotton to spandex, a far cry from the earliest socks.

452
00:32:38,361 --> 00:32:43,020
For hundreds of years, the men and women who could afford them wore long foot and leg coverings

453
00:32:43,021 --> 00:32:46,180
made typically of cotton or silk, called stockings.

454
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:51,360
But in the 19th century, as men's pants got longer, the term got shorter,

455
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:54,680
and socks became a part of our underwear vocabulary.

456
00:32:56,480 --> 00:33:00,020
This era also witnessed the rise of the first knitting mills in America,

457
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:03,820
in which machines took over the knitting work previously done by hand.

458
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:08,340
This really goes back to the 1800s.

459
00:33:08,360 --> 00:33:11,280
It was a lot faster than hand knitting, but you could knit a pair of socks in.

460
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:14,620
Basically, you could form long tubes with this.

461
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:18,280
You could make a pair of socks in two or three hours

462
00:33:18,281 --> 00:33:21,380
versus 15, 16, 17 hours doing it by hand.

463
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:27,060
Machines like this began the march toward the high-tech wizardry creating today's socks.

464
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:31,660
But making socks is one thing.

465
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:35,880
Making sure they measure up to consumer expectations is another.

466
00:33:35,881 --> 00:33:42,060
That's the job of the Hosiery Technology Center, part of Catawba Valley Community College in

467
00:33:42,061 --> 00:33:43,074
North Carolina.

468
00:33:43,075 --> 00:33:47,940
It has a team of researchers and experts who act as the watchdogs of the

469
00:33:47,941 --> 00:33:48,780
sock industry.

470
00:33:48,781 --> 00:33:53,400
The ABLE staff carefully analyzes the properties of the fibers used in socks,

471
00:33:53,401 --> 00:33:58,545
making sure that what the label says is what you get.

472
00:33:58,546 --> 00:34:02,040
One of the Technology Center's tests

473
00:34:02,041 --> 00:34:03,540
